# 16. Connect to a Specific StatefulSet Pod

A StatefulSet can provide predictable Pod DNS names through its governing Headless Service.

## DNS Format

```text
<pod-name>.<service-name>.<namespace>.svc.cluster.local
```

For the MySQL example:

```text
mysql-0.mysql-headless.default.svc.cluster.local

mysql-1.mysql-headless.default.svc.cluster.local

mysql-2.mysql-headless.default.svc.cluster.local
```

## Connect to mysql-0

```bash
nslookup mysql-0.mysql-headless.default.svc.cluster.local
```

This resolves the DNS name associated with `mysql-0` when its DNS record is available.

## Difference Between Service DNS and Pod DNS

### Headless Service DNS

```text
mysql-headless.default.svc.cluster.local
```

Returns eligible Pod IP addresses.

### Individual Pod DNS

```text
mysql-0.mysql-headless.default.svc.cluster.local
```

Resolves the address associated with `mysql-0`.

**Remember:**

Headless Service DNS = Discover multiple Pods.

Individual Pod DNS = Discover a specific Pod.

By default, readiness affects which Pod addresses appear in DNS. DNS caching can also delay updates.

