# 34. Final Summary

## Normal ClusterIP Service

```text
Client
   |
Service Virtual IP
   |
Kubernetes Service Routing
   |
Healthy Backend Pod
```

**Purpose:** Stable Service address and Kubernetes-level traffic distribution.

## Headless Service

```text
Client
   |
Headless Service DNS
   |
Pod IP Addresses
   |
Client Selects Pod
```

**Purpose:** Direct Pod discovery through DNS.

## Deployment

```text
Deployment
    |
ReplicaSet
    |
Interchangeable Pods
```

**Purpose:** Manage applications where Pods do not require stable individual identities.

## StatefulSet

```text
StatefulSet
    |
Stable Pod Identities
    |
Dedicated Persistent Storage
(when configured)
```

**Purpose:** Manage applications requiring stable identities and stateful workload features.

## Key Takeaways

**Deployment:** Any interchangeable Pod can handle the work.

**StatefulSet:** Each Pod can maintain its own stable identity.

**ClusterIP Service:** Kubernetes provides a virtual Service IP and routes traffic to backend Pods.

**Headless Service:** DNS exposes individual Pod addresses so clients can select a destination.

**PersistentVolumeClaim:** Provides persistent storage when configured with a suitable storage system.

